{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q138536173","formula":"C₉H₁₂BrNO₂","hill":"C9H12BrNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":12.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"2-OH-2C-B"},"descriptions":{"en":"2-OH-2C-B, also known as 2-O-desmethyl-2C-B (2-DM-2C-B) or as 4-bromo-2-hydroxy-5-methoxyphenethylamine (B-2-HMPEA), is a serotonin receptor modulator of the phenethylamine family related to the 2C psychedelic 2C-B (2,5-dimethoxy-4-bromophenethylamine). It is the 2-O-demethylated analogue of 2C-B. The drug is a potent agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor, with an affinity (Ki) of 0.92 nM, an EC50Tooltip half-maximal effective concentration of 4.3 nM, and an EmaxTooltip maximal efficacy of 93%. For comparison, 2C-B had an affinity (Ki) of 0.64 nM, an EC50 of 3.3 nM, and an Emax of 76%."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":84705552,"mass":246.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C=C(C(=C1)CCN)O)Br","inchikey":"LTIUWTXENMGCDK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2-aminoethyl)-5-bromo-4-methoxyphenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"84705552","atoms":25,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.386,"y":-0.811,"z":-1.416,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.183,"y":0.411,"z":-0.721,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.955,"y":0.626,"z":-0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.77,"y":1.846,"z":0.517,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.551,"y":2.156,"z":1.125,"el":"C"},{"x":0.494,"y":1.238,"z":1.07,"el":"C"},{"x":0.341,"y":0.011,"z":0.42,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.891,"y":-0.283,"z":-0.194,"el":"C"},{"x":1.476,"y":-0.984,"z":0.341,"el":"C"},{"x":2.445,"y":-0.657,"z":-0.8,"el":"C"},{"x":3.537,"y":-1.629,"z":-0.888,"el":"N"},{"x":1.696,"y":1.527,"z":1.652,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.161,"y":3.139,"z":0.627,"el":"Br"},{"x":-2.706,"y":-0.899,"z":-2.269,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.291,"y":-1.669,"z":-0.742,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.409,"y":-0.807,"z":-1.806,